ics_and_Communists_in_Twentieth-Century_Italy","details":{"publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc"],"subtitle":"Between Conflict and Dialogue","source_records":["bwb:9781350061422","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-029.mrc:119524595:1725","marc:marc_bloomsbury/2025MAR_bloomsbury.mrc:25076176:2900","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_029.bib.mrc:347758774:2675"],"title":"Catholics and Communists in Twentieth-Century Italy","number_of_pages":272,"isbn_13":["9781350061422"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["HX536","BX1396.4 .S37 2020","HX289 .S27 2019"],"publish_date":"2019","key":"/books/OL29423784M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL509948A","name":"Daniela Saresella"}],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL21645045W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"subjects":["Catholic church","Communism and christianity","Communist parties","Political parties, italy"],"oclc_numbers":["1082562435","1151391769"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Catholics and Communists in Twentieth-Century Italy explores the critical moments in the relationship between the Catholic world and the Italian left, providing unmatched insight into one of the most significant dynamics in political and religious history in Italy in the last hundred years.The book covers the Catholic Communist movement in Rome (1937-45), the experience of the Resistenza, the governmental collaboration between the Catholic Party (DC) and the Italian Communist Party (PCI) until 1947, and the dialogue between some of the key figures in both spheres in the tensest years of the Cold War. Daniela Saresella even goes on to consider the legacy that these interactions have left in Italy in the 21st century.\""},"identifiers":{"doi":["10.5040/9781350061453"]},"latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-25T17:32:05.733817"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-02-10T02:15:18.418483"}}},"ISBN:9781350145641":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781350145641","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL29486393M/Narratives_of_Disenchantment_and_Secularization","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL29486393M/Narratives_of_Disenchantment_and_Secularization","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/14091006-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc","Bloomsbury Academic"],"subtitle":"Critiquing Max Weber's Idea of Modernity","source_records":["bwb:9781350145641","amazon:1350145645","marc:marc_bloomsbury/2025MAR_bloomsbury.mrc:47562977:4469"],"title":"Narratives of Disenchantment and Secularization","number_of_pages":272,"isbn_13":["9781350145641"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["","HM477","BT82 .N373 2020eb"],"publish_date":"2020","key":"/books/OL29486393M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7071981A","name":"Robert A. Yelle"},{"key":"/authors/OL8024836A","name":"Lorenz Trein"}],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL21676723W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"covers":[14091006],"oclc_numbers":["1195717113"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"What does it really mean to be modern? The contributors to this collection offer critical attempts both to re-read Max Weber's historical idea of disenchantment and to develop further his understanding of what the contested relationship between modernity and religion represents. The approach is distinctive because it focuses on disenchantment as key to understanding those aspects of modern society and culture that Weber diagnosed. This is in opposition to approaches that focus on secularization , narrowly construed as the rise of secularism or the divide between religion and politics, and that then conflate this with modernization as a whole. Other novel contributions are discussions of temporality - meaning the sense of time or of historical change that posits a separation between an ostensibly secular modernity and its religious past - and of the manner in which such a sense of time is constructed and disseminated through narratives that themselves may resemble religious myths. It reflects the idea that disenchantment is a narrative with either Enlightenment, Romantic, or Christian roots, thereby developing a conversation between critical studies in the field of secularism (such as those of Talal Asad and Gil Anidjar) and conceptual history approaches to secularization and modernity (such as those of Karl Løwith and Reinhart Koselleck), and in the process creates something that is more than merely the sum of its parts.\"--"},"identifiers":{"doi":["10.5040/9781350145672"]},"latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-26T08:25:18.836120"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-04-30T15:23:12.059864"}}},"ISBN:9781350327757":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781350327757","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL36271246M/Narratives_of_Disenchantment_and_Secularization","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL36271246M/Narratives_of_Disenchantment_and_Secularization","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7071981A","name":"Robert A. Yelle"},{"key":"/authors/OL8024836A","name":"Lorenz Trein"}],"isbn_13":["9781350327757"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"pagination":"272","publish_date":"2022","publishers":["Bloomsbury Publishing Plc"],"source_records":["bwb:9781350327757"],"title":"Narratives of Disenchantment and Secularization","subtitle":"Critiquing Max Weber's Idea of Modernity","full_title":"Narratives of Disenchantment and Secularization Critiquing Max Weber's Idea of Modernity","works":[{"key":"/works/OL21676723W"}],"key":"/books/OL36271246M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-12-29T22:28:48.392832"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-12-29T22:28:48.392832"}}},"ISBN:9781576076781":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781576076781","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL3415502M/Puritans_and_Puritanis